  .vimeo-responsive.square {
    max-width: 90%;
  }
}
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;by keya singh and ioanna loup&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
the body provides us a sensual experience of itself, others and the world. in return, it demands care and concern – often requiring professional intervention. with its roots in mark fisher’s texts about “the eerie”, this film explores such interventions with a focus on ophthalmology and one patient’s inner voice during those interventions. the eerie is the failure of presence and the failure of absence. and our eyes contribute to these failures.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>tommy needs a haircut</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/tommy-needs-a-haircut/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 10 Mar 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/tommy-needs-a-haircut/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A series of ongoing live works centred on the world of Grand Theft Auto: Vice City. This work began in March 2024 as a playful revisitation of a nostalgic game from my childhood. I employ the protagonist, Tommy, as the actor on my stage who performs in ways that are often more sensual than originally written in the game. By doing so, I amplify the complexities of human behaviour and social dynamics within the game environment as they reflect real-world ethical dilemmas fuelled with existentialism. Inspired by Lev Manovich&amp;rsquo;s notions of media remixability, I am interested in remixing not just aesthetics but also techniques, methods, and languages of different media. For the future of this project, I want to get into subtle alterations of the game world itself.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>LyrArkestra&#43;</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/lyra/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 18 Nov 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/lyra/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;LyrArkestra+ was a collaborative project within which I created visuals along with &lt;a
  href=&#34;https://cristinamaldonado.com&#34;
    target=&#34;_blank&#34;
  &gt;Cristina&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a
  href=&#34;https://isajuchniewicz.com&#34;
    target=&#34;_blank&#34;
  &gt;Isa&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The project focused on performing graphic scores primarily by Czech and Slovak composers in unconventional audiovisual renditions. The international ensemble of this essentially fluid project does not have a permanent team. The audio composition were developed and performed by Tomáš Knoflíček (Gurun Gurun) from Ostrava, Michal Zbořil (IQ+1, B4) from Přerov, Daniel Jakeš (Jasnovidec, Koroze) from High Tatras, Ken Ganfield (PIO, The MoND) from Ames, Martin Nábělek (Boyse) from Banská Bystrica, and Petr Vrba (Poisonous Frequencies, Banausoi) from Prague. All sounds originated in the Lyra synthesizer, which is described as &amp;ldquo;organismic&amp;rdquo;, i.e. close to living organisms in its internal interactions and functioning on the basis of imaginary &amp;ldquo;conversations&amp;rdquo; between the individual modules&amp;hellip;The musical component is complemented by the visuals of Cristina Maldonado, Keya Singh and Isa Juchniewicz, who has created a structured digital environment that both responds directly to the music and allows for an additional layer of improvisation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Zangezi</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/zangezi/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 13 Nov 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/zangezi/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Zangezi is a sextet accompanied by a “visual artist&amp;rdquo; and a &amp;ldquo;sound designer&amp;rdquo; that strives for an artificial but organic sound production aesthetic.&amp;quot; As the visual artist in this sextet, I composed the live-visuals in this piece along with camera support from Hoi Man. Much of the visuals were created with live-camera input along with elements made using footage filmed the day before during our rehearsals. In this work, the visuals mainly played with temporality and multiplicity of the image.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>LAB_D&#39;epog</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/video/lab-depog/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/video/lab-depog/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;
      &lt;iframe allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen&#34; loading=&#34;eager&#34; referrerpolicy=&#34;strict-origin-when-cross-origin&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/embed/DIW8sRDWgR0?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; title=&#34;YouTube video&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

I was asked to create a video using curated archive footage by Matyaš Dlab (dramaturg) and Lucia Repasska (director) of D&amp;rsquo;epog. This work was made in collaboration with a Ukrainian artist, John Object.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The idea was to play with the infectious, chaotic energy that D&amp;rsquo;epog exudes. I decided to build the narrative around an understated metaphor of screens as an observation of self while slowing and stretching time.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Insider</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/insider/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 30 Nov 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/insider/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;floating-toc&#34; class=&#34;floating-toc&#34;&gt;
  &lt;button id=&#34;toc-toggle&#34; class=&#34;toc-toggle&#34;&gt;
    &lt;span id=&#34;toc-icon&#34;&gt;☰&lt;/span&gt; contents
  &lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;div id=&#34;toc-content&#34; class=&#34;toc-content&#34;&gt;
    &lt;nav id=&#34;toc-nav&#34;&gt;
      
      
      &lt;ul id=&#34;toc-list&#34;&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
      
    &lt;/nav&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
.floating-toc {
  position: fixed;
  right: 2rem;
  top: 120px;
  width: 280px;
  z-index: 0;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
  backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
  border: 2px solid rgb(var(--color-primary-400));
  border-radius: 0.5rem;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}

.dark .floating-toc {
  background: rgb(var(--color-neutral-800));
  border-color: rgb(var(--color-primary-600));
}

.toc-toggle {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  background: rgba(var(--color-primary-600), 0.3);
  color: white;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 0.5rem 0.5rem 0 0;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-align: left;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  transition: background 0.2s;
}

.toc-toggle:hover {
  background: rgb(var(--color-primary-700));
}

.toc-content {
  max-height: 70vh;
  overflow-y: auto;
  padding: 1rem;
  display: block;
}

.toc-content.hidden {
  display: none;
}

.floating-toc nav ul {
  list-style: none;
  padding-left: 0;
  margin: 0;
}

.floating-toc nav ul ul {
  padding-left: 1rem;
  margin-top: 0.25rem;
}

.floating-toc nav li {
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
}

.floating-toc nav a {
  color: rgb(var(--color-neutral-700));
  text-decoration: none;
  transition: color 0.2s;
  display: block;
}

.floating-toc nav a:hover {
  color: rgb(var(--color-primary-600));
}

.dark .floating-toc nav a {
  color: rgb(var(--color-neutral-300));
}

.dark .floating-toc nav a:hover {
  color: rgb(var(--color-primary-400));
}

@media (min-width: 1280px) and (max-width: 1600px) {
  .floating-toc {
    right: 1rem;
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1600px) {
  .floating-toc {
    right: calc((100vw - 1200px) / 2 - 320px);
  }
}

@media (max-width: 1280px) {
  .floating-toc {
    display: none;
  }
}

.toc-content::-webkit-scrollbar {
  width: 6px;
}

.toc-content::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
}

.toc-content::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
  border-radius: 10px;
}
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
document.addEventListener(&#39;DOMContentLoaded&#39;, function() {
  
  const toggle = document.getElementById(&#39;toc-toggle&#39;);
  const content = document.getElementById(&#39;toc-content&#39;);
  const icon = document.getElementById(&#39;toc-icon&#39;);

  if (toggle &amp;&amp; content &amp;&amp; icon) {
    toggle.addEventListener(&#39;click&#39;, function() {
      content.classList.toggle(&#39;hidden&#39;);
      icon.textContent = content.classList.contains(&#39;hidden&#39;) ? &#39;☰&#39; : &#39;✕&#39;;
    });
  }

  
  const tocList = document.getElementById(&#39;toc-list&#39;);

  if (tocList) {
    const contentArea = document.querySelector(&#39;.project-content, article, main&#39;);
    if (!contentArea) return;

    
    const predefinedSections = [
      { id: &#39;about&#39;, label: &#39;About&#39; },
      { id: &#39;process&#39;, label: &#39;Process&#39; },
      { id: &#39;documentation&#39;, label: &#39;Documentation&#39; },
      { id: &#39;press&#39;, label: &#39;Press&#39; },
      { id: &#39;credits&#39;, label: &#39;Credits&#39; },
      { id: &#39;related&#39;, label: &#39;Related&#39; }
    ];

    
    predefinedSections.forEach(function(section) {
      const element = document.getElementById(section.id);
      if (element) {
        const li = document.createElement(&#39;li&#39;);
        li.id = section.id + &#39;-item&#39;;
        const link = document.createElement(&#39;a&#39;);
        link.href = &#39;#&#39; + section.id;
        link.textContent = section.label;
        li.appendChild(link);
        tocList.appendChild(li);
      }
    });

    
    const headings = contentArea.querySelectorAll(&#39;h2&#39;);
    const predefinedIds = predefinedSections.map(s =&gt; s.id);

    headings.forEach(function(heading) {
      
      if (!heading.id) {
        heading.id = heading.textContent.toLowerCase()
          .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, &#39;-&#39;)
          .replace(/(^-|-$)/g, &#39;&#39;);
      }

      
      if (predefinedIds.includes(heading.id)) {
        return;
      }

      
      const li = document.createElement(&#39;li&#39;);
      const link = document.createElement(&#39;a&#39;);
      link.href = &#39;#&#39; + heading.id;
      link.textContent = heading.textContent;
      li.appendChild(link);
      tocList.appendChild(li);
    });

    
    const galleries = document.querySelectorAll(&#39;.gallery-box h3&#39;);
    const documentationItem = document.getElementById(&#39;documentation-item&#39;);

    if (galleries.length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; documentationItem) {
      const submenu = document.createElement(&#39;ul&#39;);
      galleries.forEach(function(gallery, index) {
        const title = gallery.textContent;
        const anchor = &#39;gallery-&#39; + index;
        gallery.id = anchor;

        const li = document.createElement(&#39;li&#39;);
        const link = document.createElement(&#39;a&#39;);
        link.href = &#39;#&#39; + anchor;
        link.textContent = title;
        li.appendChild(link);
        submenu.appendChild(li);
      });

      documentationItem.appendChild(submenu);
    }
  } else {
    
    const tocNav = document.querySelector(&#39;#toc-nav&#39;);
    if (tocNav) {
      const blogGalleries = document.querySelectorAll(&#39;.blog-gallery-box h3&#39;);

      if (blogGalleries.length &gt; 0) {
        let blogTocList = tocNav.querySelector(&#39;ul&#39;);
        if (!blogTocList) {
          blogTocList = document.createElement(&#39;ul&#39;);
          tocNav.appendChild(blogTocList);
        }

        blogGalleries.forEach(function(gallery, index) {
          const title = gallery.textContent;
          if (!gallery.id) {
            gallery.id = &#39;blog-gallery-&#39; + index;
          }

          const li = document.createElement(&#39;li&#39;);
          const link = document.createElement(&#39;a&#39;);
          link.href = &#39;#&#39; + gallery.id;
          link.textContent = title;
          li.appendChild(link);
          blogTocList.appendChild(li);
        });
      }
    }
  }
});
&lt;/script&gt;


&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;About
    &lt;div id=&#34;about&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#about&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;
    
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Insider is a mixed reality performative exploration of the senses focusing on notions of embodiment and body ownership. It&amp;rsquo;s a performance for 1 audience member at a time. Each audience member is accompanied by a performer who facilitates the experience. Choices made by the audience members can create unique experiences for each person who sees this work.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Insider: unwrapping reality/opening</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/neither/insider-unwrapping/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 30 Nov 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/neither/insider-unwrapping/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We have adapted &lt;a
  href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/projects/live/insider&#34;&gt;Insider&lt;/a&gt; into installations for opening events to reach audiences outside the performance schedules. Each installation explores various elements of the work while adapting to the theme of the hosting event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These installations were created by a collective of artists - Cristina Maldonado, Keya Singh, Eva Rosemarijn, Lea Kukovičič, Isa Juchniewicz, Lamija Čehajić. Our individual participation at each event changes as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;gallery-box border-4 border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 rounded-lg p-6 my-4&#34;&gt;
  
  &lt;h3 class=&#34;gallery-title text-xl font-bold mb-1&#34;&gt;Premiere at CED with Terén&lt;/h3&gt;
  

  
  &lt;p class=&#34;gallery-location text-sm mb-2&#34;&gt;
    
    
    28/11/19, Brno, CZ
  &lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
